  "raw": " types.\n\nHowever, the blood shortage across the UK could hit some NHS blood units that have patients from across the Europe, as Britain is the only country outside the European Union that has so few blood units for everyone.\n\nA spokesperson for Blood Donor Services, an NHSBT service, said: \"We are seeing a number of blood units, blood banks and whole facilities going over and above in order to meet demand. The O negative unit has been under pressure for some time – there is a shortage of units, but they are all on standby. We are going to be bringing some over here temporarily this week and the supply chain is working overtime.\"\n\nA spokesperson for NHSBT said all blood types were needed and urged people to donate regularly.\n\nThe spokesperson said NHSBT has a policy that aims to meet demand and help supply units. For patients, they were more likely to find themselves in hospital if they had a blood group O negative than blood group O.\n\n",
  "serialized": "types. However, the blood shortage across the UK could hit some NHS blood units that have patients from across the Europe, as Britain is the only country outside the European Union that has so few blood units for everyone. A spokesperson for Blood Donor Services, an NHSBT service, said: \"We are seeing a number of blood units, blood banks and whole facilities going over and above in order to meet demand. The O negative unit has been under pressure for some time – there is a shortage of units, but they are all on standby. We are going to be bringing some over here temporarily this week and the supply chain is working overtime.\" A spokesperson for NHSBT said all blood types were needed and urged people to donate regularly. The spokesperson said NHSBT has a policy that aims to meet demand and help supply units. For patients, they were more likely to find themselves in hospital if they had a blood group O negative than blood group O.",
